        'Ravenstein\'s Laws of Migration (1885): most migrants move short distances; migration occurs in steps; long-distance migrants prefer major economic centres; rural dwellers migrate more than urban; females dominate short-distance moves; migration increases with economic development; every migration stream produces a counter-stream.',
